From 6860289304dc5e304ddc867900c6747f14119605 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergio Villar Senin <svillar@igalia.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 13:47:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Do not size the content to the screen when entering DOM
 fullscreen

nsDOMWindowUtils::HandleFullscreenRequests() sets the size of the content
viewer to the screen size right before entering fullscreen, expecting the
widget to be resized to the screen too. That is not the case in Wolvic, where
the widget is the surface the content is rendered to and keeps its size in
fullscreen: the content is laid out at the screen size, which is larger than
the surface, and the part that does not fit is cropped.

The size is read once from the content process' screen, so changing the
screen size after the fullscreen request does not fix it, and there is no
ordering guarantee between a screen update and the request.

Skip that step so the viewer keeps the size of the widget, which is what the
content has to fill. Nothing needs to be restored on exit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dom/base/nsDOMWindowUtils.cpp | 8 +++-----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dom/base/nsDOMWindowUtils.cpp b/dom/base/nsDOMWindowUtils.cpp
index 73ffc2e..fc79a18 100644
--- a/dom/base/nsDOMWindowUtils.cpp
+++ b/dom/base/nsDOMWindowUtils.cpp
@@ -3548,12 +3548,10 @@ nsDOMWindowUtils::HandleFullscreenRequests(bool* aRetVal) {
   // set the window dimensions in advance. Since the resize message
   // comes after the fullscreen change call, doing so could avoid an
   // extra resize reflow after this point.
-  nsRect screenRect;
-  if (nsPresContext* presContext = GetPresContext()) {
-    screenRect = presContext->DeviceContext()->GetRect();
-  }
+  // Do not use the screen size here: in Wolvic the widget is the surface the
+  // content is rendered to and it keeps its size in fullscreen.
   nsSize oldSize;
-  PrepareForFullscreenChange(GetDocShell(), screenRect.Size(), &oldSize);
+  PrepareForFullscreenChange(GetDocShell(), nsSize(), &oldSize);
   OldWindowSize::Set(mWindow, oldSize);
 
   *aRetVal = Document::HandlePendingFullscreenRequests(doc);
